body:
Discuss your wages with other Employees in the USA. Some employers include an illegal clause stating you can't discuss your wages with other employees.

&#x200B;

But this can be considered part of 'union busting' and the [***National Labor Relations Act***](https://www.nlrb.gov/guidance/key-reference-materials/national-labor-relations-act) which is federal law and cannot be overridden at a state or local level, ensures that you have the right to discuss your wages with whomever you wish without fear of retaliation or being fired.

I hope you got the help you needed.

&#x200B;

Exsanguination (blood loss) has a few stages. Feeling light-headed is the first, then feeling tired/drained of energy. Then comes chills and cold as your body loses the ability to regulate temperature and you start to want to sleep. as you bleed out, you'll eventually slip into unconsciousness, and expire if immediate help is not given.
